index 41f6665..5cefdd9 100644
--- a/src/channels/docs/adapters.md
+++ b/src/channels/docs/adapters.md
@@ -31,3 +31,38 @@ Microsoft Teams ([msteams-channel](../msteams/msteams-channel.ts), ATO-506) uses
 Shared model commands currently import provider persistence from TUI; stage 02 moves that responsibility. Do not describe this boundary as already repaired.
 
 Sources: [Telegram](../telegram/telegram-channel.ts), [Discord](../discord/discord-channel.ts), [Swarm](../swarm/swarm-registry.ts), [model commands](../model-command.ts), [backoff](../reconnect-backoff.ts). Tests: [Telegram](../telegram/telegram-channel.test.ts), [cron](../telegram/cron-command.test.ts), [Discord](../discord/discord-channel.test.ts), [model commands](../telegram/inbound-model-command.test.ts).
+
+## Desktop session continuation
+
+TUI turns mark their session with `metadata.desktopTelegramBridge` inside the FIFO
+callback, after reloading saved state. The legacy `macTelegramBridge` marker is
+accepted when reading existing sessions. The bridge uses platform-neutral runtime APIs. The paired owner's
+private Telegram DM may connect through `/desktop [session-id]` (`/mac` is an
+alias). With no ID it picks the only running marked session, or the most recent
+marked session when all are idle. Multiple running sessions require an explicit
+ID. Incognito sessions and other channels are excluded.
+
+`/status` and `/result` read the selected session without inference. English
+natural-language equivalents include “How far along are you?” and “Show me the
+result of your analysis”. Legacy German input phrases remain accepted. Control
+messages are English, and follow-up turns request English replies. Stored answers
+and plan text are returned verbatim, preserving the original analysis.
+
+Other messages and `/queue <request>` use the same session's FIFO `runtime.runTurn`,
+waiting for current work and reloading saved context at the queue boundary.
+Several requests may be outstanding per chat. A serial queue tracks their abort
+signals and size while status/result messages bypass execution. Approvals bind on the remote turn's first event and
+release on its terminal event and in cleanup. Status reads and queued requests
+do not move a desktop turn's approval route. A stored active turn that this
+runtime does not own must be resumed in this terminal before a remote follow-up.
+
+`/desktop off` or `/new` returns the private chat to its own Telegram conversation.
+The terminal process must stay running; this feature does not connect separate
+Atomic processes or start a desktop session on another computer.
+
+`/cancel` cancels outstanding Telegram requests. `/stop` also calls the runtime
+turn controller's cancellation hook for the currently owning desktop turn.
+Hooks are installed only while a submission owns its session and removed at
+settlement. The runtime combines its cancellation signal with the caller's
+signal. Tool cancellation remains cooperative, preserving completed effects.
+Channel shutdown cancels all remote queues before stopping its active turns.
